"tour theming" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		Tour
		<header>A tour leads someone through a feature one numbered step at a time, pointing at what each step is about.</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Set a public `--ui-*` token on the element, any ancestor or `:root`; it inherits into the shadow
			root. Edit a value below to try it.
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-tour" playground>
				<ui-stack class="ui-stack">
					<ui-stack class="ui-cluster">
						<ui-button id="tour-new-playground" icon="plus">New</>
						<ui-button id="tour-save-playground" icon="save">Save</>
						<ui-button commandfor="tour-example-playground" command="--start" appearance="basic" icon="map signs">Take the tour</>
					</>
					<ui-tour id="tour-example-playground" name="The toolbar" summary="What its buttons do.">
						<ui-tour-step target="tour-new">New starts a fresh page.</>
						<ui-tour-step name="save" target="tour-save" dim>Save keeps what you've done.</>
						<ui-tour-step>That's it. You can take this tour again any time.</>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
